{offset200}{ia1}{offset0}

{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}

Linz









Magnus Von Tekton, the monster, fold back on his eagle's nest, {arialbld}Tektonstein{arial}{pause}

Magnus had this fortress built over ten years in a high valley in the heart of Kragenberg's imposing mountains. The site is uniquely accessible from three narrow gaps littered with bunkers cut inside the rock itself. To the north is the Walkyries gap, to the east the Frankenstein pass and to the south the gate of Tannäuzer. Naturally each of these passes is guarded by an armored division.{pause}

Flight over this zone is forbidden by the numerous nests of flaks placed on the ridges, to say nothing about the cream of Psycho fighters assigned to the site's three air fields.{pause}

We also know that Tektonstein provides facilities for manufacturing flying bombs as well as functional launching ramps.{pause}

If you ask me how we're going to get in this armored coffin, I'll tell you we can't. The High Commandment says the same: Tektonstein is impregnable, with conventional weapons...{pause}

I'm going to tell you a secret {name}, our very own eggheads in white smocks have long worked on this bomb, you know "the bomb", the nuke thing, I know they call it the "Atonic" bomb.{pause}


{arialbld}CONFIDENTIAL{arial}{pause}













{center}{device36}












{pause}A little bird also told me that your prime minister Weston Lacoline and my president Clarissa Jackson are currently sounding out whether they'll have to wait for this damned miracle bomb which clean up all problems with a big whoosh...{pause}

And while these ladies and gentlemen are deciding on the device's color our good old daddy Magnus Von Tekton can enjoy himself another few months in his Master of the World outfit!{pause}

We haven't come this far to be replaced at the last moment by some bloody "apparatus". Even though he's a Parano degenerate, Sakharin is with me.{pause}

Remember what T-Rex's father, General Theodore Spirex, said: "War is much too important to be left to the politicians".{pause}

We will show these pen-pushers how battle must be fought: with "audace", "panache" and that "triumph without peril brings no glory".{pause}

That bastard Sakharin is in, only you are left {arialbld}{name}!{arial} Are you up for it pal?{pause}

This mission, if you accept it, could well be our last, then come at the gate of Tannäuzer and don't be late {rank}.{pause}



{offset100}Commander of the 3rd Schyzo Army

{offset150}{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}



